# Omni Provider

Manages [Omni Analytics](https://omni.co) through the [Omni REST API](https://docs.omni.co/api).

The provider covers the parts of an Omni instance that belong in version control: database
connections, shared and extension models, the model YAML that defines topics and views, content
folders, and the users, groups, and role assignments that decide who can see what.

## Example usage

```terraform
terraform {
  required_providers {
    omni = {
      source  = "ashima-omni/omni"
      version = "~> 0.1"
    }
  }
}

provider "omni" {
  base_url  = "https://blobsrus.omniapp.co"
  api_token = var.omni_api_token
}

resource "omni_connection" "warehouse" {
  name      = "Production Snowflake"
  dialect   = "snowflake"
  host      = "myaccount"
  database  = "ANALYTICS"
  warehouse = "COMPUTE_WH"
  username  = "OMNI_SVC"
  password  = var.snowflake_password
  base_role = "NO_ACCESS"
}
```

## Authentication

Generate a token in Omni under **Settings > API keys**, then supply it as `api_token` or through
the `OMNI_API_TOKEN` environment variable.

Omni has two token types and they are not interchangeable:

| Token type            | Use it for                                                                 |
| --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Organization API key  | Everything, including `omni_user` and `omni_user_group` (SCIM endpoints)    |
| Personal access token | Connections, models, model YAML, folders, and role assignments              |

Run the provider with an organization API key if you manage users or groups.

## Base URL

`base_url` is the URL you log in with, for example `https://blobsrus.omniapp.co`. The provider
appends `/api` itself, so both forms work. Set it with the `OMNI_BASE_URL` environment variable
in CI.

## Rate limits

The Omni API allows 60 requests per minute. The provider retries `429` and `5xx` responses with
exponential backoff. For large configurations, `terraform apply -parallelism=5` keeps applies
comfortably inside the limit.

